{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "ISA",
  "chapter": 16,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "ISA.16.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.16.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Send ye the lamb to the ruler of the land from Sela to the wilderness, to the mount of the daughter of Zion.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.16.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.16.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For it shall be, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", as a wandering bird cast out of the nest, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "so",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the daughters of Moab shall be at the fords of Arnon.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.16.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.16.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Take counsel, execute judgment; make thy shadow as the night in the midst of the noon-day; hide the outcasts; discover not him that wandereth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.16.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.16.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let my outcasts dwell with thee, Moab; be thou a covert to them from the face of the spoiler: for the extortioner is at an end, the spoiler ceaseth, the oppressors are consumed out of the land.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.16.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.16.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And in mercy shall the throne be established: and he shall sit upon it in truth in the tabernacle of David, judging, and seeking judgment, and hasting righteousness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.16.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.16.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "We have heard of the pride of Moab; ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "he is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " very proud: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of his haughtiness, and his pride, and his wrath: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "but",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " his lies ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shall",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " so.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.16.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.16.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore shall Moab howl for Moab, every one shall howl: for the foundations of Kir-hareseth shall ye mourn; surely ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "they are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " stricken.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.16.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.16.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the fields of Heshbon languish, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the vine of Sibmah: the lords of the heathen have broken down her principal plants, they have come ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to Jazer, they wandered ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "through",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the wilderness: her branches are extended, they have gone over the sea.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.16.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.16.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore I will bewail with the weeping of Jazer the vine of Sibmah: I will water thee with my tears, O Heshbon, and Elealeh: for the shouting for thy summer fruits and for thy harvest is fallen.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.16.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.16.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And gladness is taken away, and joy from the plentiful field; and in the vineyards there shall be no singing, neither shall there be shouting: the treaders shall tread out no wine in ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "their",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " presses; I have made ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "their vintage",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " -shouting to cease.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.16.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.16.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wherefore my bowels shall sound like a harp for Moab, and my inward parts for Kir-haresh.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.16.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.16.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And it shall come to pass, when it is seen that Moab is weary on the high place, that he shall come to his sanctuary to pray; but he shall not prevail.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.16.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.16.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "This ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the word that the LORD hath spoken concerning Moab since that time.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.16.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.16.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But now the LORD hath spoken, saying, Within three years, as the years of a hireling, and the glory of Moab shall be contemned, with all that great multitude; and the remnant ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shall be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " very small ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " feeble.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
